{
  "repository": "https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness",
  "changes": [
    "Source revisions are pinned per file. Import aliases target the selected local closure.",
    "ScopedStandardSourceBinding.ctx is an opaque RSI object instead of a Cordis Context.",
    "Dockkit keeps upstream geometry and gestures; imports use its local primitive closure. exports.ts is an RSI import adapter.",
    "Menu accepts an explicit portal container so navigation actions opened in a native modal stay in its interactive layer. A navigation row can identify the current destination through MenuRow.",
    "Product SVG artwork and icon components are unchanged. The RSI root mounts the static sprite; no DSH brand or font assets are imported.",
    "theme-base.css omits the unused brand font declaration; system text/code fonts and focus rules remain.",
    "dockkit-tokens.css adapts the platform palette and menu fills to RSI appearance selectors, repeats dark declarations for system appearance, and omits unused token families.",
    "slots/index.ts exposes the keyed Hook member overload already implemented by renderer/bindings.tsx.",
    "TabLayout releases scroll offsets when their pane is removed, after child strip cleanup; TabPanel documents this bounded lifetime.",
    "Split separators and floating move/resize controls expose host-owned accessible labels, bounded keyboard intents and visible focus boxes; undo uses the existing intent history.",
    "Keyboard float resizing preserves the engine minimum even when End fills a viewport edge smaller than that minimum.",
    "TrajectoryTimeline keeps the upstream gesture, accessibility and time projections. Its record, layout and English translation contracts include only the fields used by the timeline.",
    "The Schedule catalog uses the upstream recommendation artwork, English recommendation copy and tile styling. The task click opens the local starting draft.",
    "TextSearchIndex retains the upstream multilingual matching and ranking. The task manager builds it on the first search and releases it when cleared. Its closure omits localization helpers and cross-index preparation caches.",
    "typography.css keeps the font shorthands used by the Web components and the code font size adjustment.",
    "The resource guide uses upstream card styling and the Files, Terminal, More tools and compass artwork. Only mounted glyphs are included.",
    "AttachmentRail accepts the composer's keyed children and item count. Its styles retain the rail and paging controls.",
    "Background job rows use the upstream section styles and terminal block. Terminal copy uses the document clipboard bridge.",
    "Quote selection uses the upstream DOM text projection, gesture placement, button styles and Markdown formatter. Its hook includes only the upstream interaction types it consumes.",
    "Entered message images use the upstream gallery stylesheet and single-image size calculation. The owner supplies pane-bound Media reads and its shared image dialog."
  ],
